WEBVTT

00:07:01.375 --> 00:07:04.545
So we can also reverse-engineer
where dark matter is --

00:07:04.587 --> 00:07:07.381
it's represented here
by the bluish purple.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:11.510
We can look at how images
of galaxy clusters

00:07:11.552 --> 00:07:13.429
are distorted, which tells us something

00:07:13.429 --> 00:07:16.140
about how dark matter
is distorting space-time.

00:07:17.266 --> 00:07:21.562
So we know something
about how much dark matter there is,

00:07:21.562 --> 00:07:24.982
and even how the dark matter
is distributed,

00:07:25.024 --> 00:07:27.276
but what kind of particle is it?

00:07:28.527 --> 00:07:29.778
So all that we know

00:07:29.778 --> 00:07:32.781
is that it's beyond
standard-model physics.